# User Profile & Settings — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Design and implement a role-tailored User Profile & Settings module conforming to IQArchive's institutional design system (DaisyUI + Tailwind CSS v4 + Inertia.js Vue 3), prioritizing the **IQA Member / Staff** interface first as the flagship accreditation authority view.
- Scope:
  - In scope (Phase 1 — IQA Member Interface First):
    - Interactive Profile & Account Settings view at `/settings`, tailored primarily for IQA Staff (`iqa_staff` / `iqa_member`).
    - Dedicated IQA University-Wide Scope & Governance card (all colleges, active survey monitoring).
    - IQA Workstation Preferences (document matrix density, human-in-the-loop OCR review threshold, default landing workspace).
    - Accreditation Alert Routing (dean endorsements, deficit alerts, survey milestone reminders).
    - Institutional Security & Audit Footprint card (Google SSO read-only lock banner, recent audit trail from `audit_logs`).
    - Backend data orchestration in `AuthController::settings()` or dedicated `UserProfileController` returning typed props for IQA users.
    - Modular architecture under 150 lines per Vue component (DaisyUI `card`, `badge`, `toggle`, `tabs`, `table`, `btn`).
  - In scope (Phase 2 & Phase 3 — Remaining Roles):
    - Phase 2: College Dean (single-college scope, dean approval alerts) and Task Force Member (program + assigned area parameters, upload defaults).
    - Phase 3: External/Internal Accreditors (read-only evaluation matrix, visit window), BU Executive (KPI digests), System Administrator (tenant & log administration).
  - Out of scope:
    - Modifying Google Workspace passwords or SSO credentials (centrally managed by BU ICTO).
    - Direct database schema modifications unless non-breaking user preference JSON columns or defaults are needed.

## Role Component Comparison Matrix

| Component Section | IQA Member (Phase 1 Priority) | College Dean (Phase 2) | Task Force Member (Phase 2) | Accreditors (Phase 3) | BU Executive / Admin (Phase 3) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Profile Identity** | Institutional email, IQA Staff badge, QA Officer designation, Google SSO verified lock | Institutional email, Dean badge, College affiliation badge | Institutional email, Faculty / TF badge, College & Program pill | Institutional email, Accreditor badge, Affiliated Agency / Team | Executive / SysAdmin badge, University Seal |
| **Authority & Scope** | **University-Wide (All Colleges & Programs)**; Active survey monitoring counter | **Single College Scope** (e.g. College of Science); Program roster under college | **Program & Area Scope** (e.g. BSCS Area III & VIII); Assigned parameters | **Survey Visit Instrument Scope** (Active accreditation instrument & assigned areas) | University-wide strategic governance / System-wide infrastructure |
| **Workstation Preferences** | Table density toggle (compact/comfortable), OCR validation threshold (e.g. 80%), default launch workspace (`/iqa`, `/documents`, `/documents/program-accreditation`) | Approval queue view mode, Endorsement signature preset | Evidence upload format defaults, OCR auto-tagging preview toggle | Rating scale display density, evidence pane split-view mode | Executive scorecard chart type, export file format preset (PDF/Excel) |
| **Notification Routing** | Dean submissions pending IQA endorsement, Task Force deficit alerts, AACCUP visit reminders | Evidence submitted for Dean approval, compliance deadlines | Area deficit alerts, review feedback from Dean/IQA | Survey evaluation schedule, team consensus meetings | Monthly accreditation board summary, strategic KPI milestone alerts |
| **Security & Activity** | Google SSO status, Last 5 IQA endorsement & validation audit events | Google SSO status, Last 5 college endorsements | Google SSO status, Last 5 evidence uploads | Google SSO status, Session expiry countdown | Google SSO status, Security log audit summary |

## Key Architectural & Design Decisions
1. **IQA Member as Reference Implementation**: Build the core shell and all partials tailored to the IQA member first. Subsequent roles will plug into the same shell via role adapters and conditional slots.
2. **Modular File Size Cap (< 150 lines)**:
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/AccountSettings.vue`: Master container, responsive layout, tab switcher (< 140 lines).
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/Partials/ProfileHeader.vue`: Institutional identity banner, avatar, verified Google SSO badge (< 90 lines).
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/Partials/IqaScopeCard.vue`: University-wide oversight scope, active cycle stats (< 110 lines).
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/Partials/IqaWorkstationPreferences.vue`: Document table density, OCR review threshold, default workspace (< 130 lines).
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/Partials/NotificationPreferences.vue`: Toggle alerts for endorsements, deficits, visit milestones (< 120 lines).
   - `resources/js/Pages/Auth/Partials/SecurityAuditCard.vue`: Central SSO notice, recent audit trail (< 120 lines).
3. **Institutional Design Tokens**: Strictly follow `DESIGN.md` (Navy `#0B1B3D`, BU Blue `#0038A8`, BU Orange `#F26522`, DaisyUI `card`, `badge`, `toggle`, `btn`, `alert`).

## Edge Cases to Handle
- IQA user with no specific `college_id` (must gracefully display "University-Wide Access (All Colleges & Campuses)").
- Dual-role IQA users (e.g. `iqa-staff-multi` with IQA Staff + Task Force Member) showing dual badges and primary workspace switch.
- Missing avatar fallbacks with stylized institutional initials (Navy/Orange).
- Empty audit log states with calm institutional placeholder copy.

## Testing Strategy
- Feature tests in `tests/Feature/UserProfileSettingsTest.php`:
  - Gated route: Unauthenticated requests to `/settings` redirect to `/login`.
  - Authenticated IQA Staff receives full profile, university-wide scope, preferences, and recent audit logs.
- Frontend build validation: `npm run build` must compile with zero errors.
- Visual inspection via browser subagent at `/dev/login/iqa-staff` -> `/settings` on desktop viewport (1440x900).

